---
import TextPage from '../../views/TextPage.astro';
import { company } from '../../data/company';
import { path } from '../../i18n/routes';
---

<TextPage
	route="about"
	heading="About us"
	lead="Jangol is a Colombian software house. We build platforms for gyms and schools, and develop custom software."
	pageType="AboutPage"
>
	<p>
		We build software for businesses that run on spreadsheets, notebooks and WhatsApp groups today. Gyms and schools share the same
		problems: nobody knows for sure who is up to date with payments, lines form at the front desk or the school office, and the same
		information is copied by hand from one place to another. For them we built
		<a href={path('gyms', 'en')}>Jangol for Gyms</a> and <a href={path('schools', 'en')}>Jangol for Schools</a>.
	</p>
	<p>
		Both platforms share the same base of accounts, payments and permissions, and they are built for how business works in Colombia:
		payments with PSE, Nequi and Daviplata, DIAN electronic invoicing and, for schools, the Decreto 1290 grading scale and SIMAT reporting.
	</p>
	<p>
		When a business needs something no platform covers, we <a href={path('custom', 'en')}>build it as custom software</a>. The same team
		defines the scope, designs, writes the code and maintains the product after launch.
	</p>

	<h2>How we work</h2>
	<p>
		We talk about your operation first and technology second. We deliver progress every two weeks in an environment where you can use it,
		and support comes from the same team that builds. In our <a href={path('resources', 'en')}>guides</a> we share what we learn working
		with our clients day to day.
	</p>

	<h2>Company details</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Company name: {company.legalName}</li>
		<li>Tax ID (NIT): {company.nit}</li>
		<li>Founded: {company.foundingYear}</li>
		<li>Founding team: {company.founders.join(', ')}</li>
		<li>Location: {company.city}, {company.country}</li>
		<li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a></li>
	</ul>
	<p>Want to meet us? <a href={path('contact', 'en')}>Book a demo or tell us your idea</a>.</p>
</TextPage>
